hobbes-leviathan-2.logic.r1: argue/answered: U1: answered yes, which keeps hobbes-leviathan-2.logic.r1 and hobbes-leviathan-2.logic.r1.3, to: Does the text's argument take this for granted, whether or not it says so: "if the Interpreter of written Lawes is the ordinary Judges, then the Judges' Sentences are to be taken by them that plead for Lawes in that particular case"? Answer yes if the author would accept it as part of the argument. [in 1 of 2 runs]
